<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n45003" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔρυθμ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, 
			Ep.
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐΰρρ</span>- <i><span class="en">
			Man.
			1.60
		</span></i>:—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>rhythmical</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μουσικὴ
			εὔ</span>., distd. fr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐμελής</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pol.</u>
				1341b26
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λέξις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Rh.</u>
					1409a21
				</span></i>
			; opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔνρυθμος</span>, <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				<u>Comp.</u>
				11
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				25
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔ. κρούματα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Th.</u>
					121
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔ. πούς</span>
			<i>moving in time, keeping time</i>, ib.<i><span class="en">
				985
			</span></i> (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προβήματα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Pl.</u>
					759
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέλος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					655a
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κίνησις</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				795e
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σφυγμὸς εὔ</span>. a
				<i>regular</i> pulse, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				19.409
			</span></i>. Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μως</span>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, καὶ μουσικῶς εἰπεῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Isoc.
					13.16
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φέρεσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.45e
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of persons,
				<i>orderly, graceful</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Prt.</u>
				326b
			</span></i> (
				Comp.
			), <i><span class="en">
				<u>R.</u>
				413e
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔ. βακτηρία</span>
				'<i>the nice conduct of</i> a cane', <i><span class="en">
				Antiph.
				33.4
			</span></i>. Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μως</span>
			<i>gracefully</i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Cyc.</u>
				563
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πέμπειν εὐ. τὸν κότταβον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.Com.
					47
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>well-proportioned, well-fitted</i>, both of the armourand the
			body, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Mem.</u>
				3.10.10
			</span></i> (
				Comp.
			), <i><span class="en">
				11
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν πόδα -ότερον τοῦ ὑποδήματος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thphr.
					<u>Char.</u>
					2.7
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔ. ὀρνίθιον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>HA</u>
					592b24
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φύλλα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thphr.
					<u>HP</u>
					3.18.7
				</span></i>
			 (
				Comp.
			), cf. <i><span class="en">
				12.9
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b> of surgical
			operations, in Adv., <i>neatly</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Off.</u>
				4
			</span></i>.</div>
